# Linear Task Template

Use this structure when creating or updating Linear issues so that context, scope, and implementation hints are clear.

## Template Structure

**🎯 Context**

Describe what needs to be done and why this matters to the user or the company.


**✅ Acceptance Criteria**

- [ ] Step 1  
- [ ] Step 2  
- [ ] Test/Validate X  


**🔗 Implementation Notes**

e.g. I think we can use Library X so we don't have to build this from scratch.

---

## Labels

Assign the correct label to each issue based on its type:

| Label | Use For |
|-------|---------|
| **Bug** | Fixes for incorrect behavior, bugs, regressions |
| **Feature** | New functionality, UI changes, enhancements |
| **Business** | Credit logic, billing, subscription, product rules |
| **QA** | Quality assurance, prompt review, accuracy validation |
| **Marketing** | Marketing-related tasks, campaigns, copy |

---

## Rules

- **Icons:** Use 🎯 (Context), ✅ (Acceptance Criteria), 🔗 (Implementation Notes) as section headers.
- **Spacing:** Add a blank line after each section header and a blank line between each of the three sections (Context, Acceptance Criteria, Implementation Notes).
- **Acceptance criteria** are checkboxes in Linear (use `- [ ]` in descriptions so they render as unchecked).
- **Labels** are required; assign one of Bug, Feature, Business, QA, or Marketing per task.
- Keep context brief but sufficient for anyone picking up the task.
- Implementation notes are optional but encouraged when they unblock or guide implementation.
